  "summary_en": "Dubai Health Authority policy setting regulatory and ethical requirements for AI solutions in healthcare in Dubai. It covers ethics, accountability, transparency, safety, privacy, minimum tool requirements, duties of developers, end users and insurers, and DHA monitoring and sanctions. It is not specific to robots.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "AI solutions must be fair, bias-free, and have built-in appeals procedures",
   "Mandatory disclosure of AI functions, validation, datasets and limitations, plus independent third-party validation",
   "High-impact AI decisions must be overridable by designated end users",
   "AI tools need graceful degradation, certification and auditable validation statements",
   "End users must report incidents to DHA-HRS and undergo independent audits; DHA imposes sanctions for breaches"
